  "reason": "Evidence: We have one RNA-only baseline (config_001: pca_n2000, singleprofile) at 0.485 accuracy. We have no information about whether image features carry any signal for this task. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) establishes the image-only baseline, which is the second critical reference point needed before evaluating multimodal fusion. Why this is best: Without knowing the image baseline, I cannot judge whether multimodal configurations (configs 016-051) are worthwhile or whether the image modality is simply noisy. This single, clean experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty in the remaining search space. ResNet50 with singleprofile keeps the comparison simple and directly analogous to the RNA baseline, isolating the effect of modality. With 8 experiments left, establishing both unimodal baselines early allows informed allocation of remaining budget to fusion strategies, encoders, and profile settings."
